# KSI-MLA: Security Monitoring and Event Management
# Validates that ExampleOrg operates a compliant SIEM capability:
# - GuardDuty: enabled, required features active, publishing findings to encrypted S3
# - SecurityHub: enabled, FSBP and NIST 800-53 standards active, cross-region aggregation
# - Security findings S3 bucket: encrypted, versioned, SSL-enforced, tamper-resistant

META
    # === Required ===
    esp_id `ksi-mla-security-monitoring-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `aws`
    criticality `critical`

    # === Documentation ===
    title `KSI-MLA: Security Monitoring and Event Management`
    description `Validates GuardDuty threat detection, Security Hub posture management, and the tamper-resistant security findings bucket collectively satisfy KSI-MLA-OSM, KSI-MLA-LET, and KSI-MLA-RVL`
    author `example-security`
    tags `aws,guardduty,securityhub,s3,siem,monitoring,fedramp,KSI-MLA-OSM,KSI-MLA-LET,KSI-MLA-RVL`

    # === Control Mapping ===
    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-MLA-OSM,KSI:KSI-MLA-LET,KSI:KSI-MLA-RVL`
    control_objective `KSI-MLA-OSM,KSI-MLA-LET,KSI-MLA-RVL`

    # === Assessment ===
    assessment_method `TEST`

    # === Implementation ===
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    # === Inheritance ===
    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `AWS:us-east-1:security-infrastructure`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    # === Remediation ===
    remediation_days `1`
    recommendation `Enable GuardDuty and Security Hub immediately. Ensure the security findings S3 bucket has KMS encryption, versioning, and a DenyNonSSL bucket policy.`

    # === Component ===
    component_id `comp-aws-security`

    # === Implementation Narratives ===
    impl_KSI_MLA_LET `Event type logging is validated by confirming GuardDuty has the following detection features in ENABLED status: CLOUD_TRAIL, DNS_LOGS, FLOW_LOGS, S3_DATA_EVENTS, and EBS_MALWARE_PROTECTION. Security Hub is validated to have AWS Foundational Security Best Practices and NIST SP 800-53 standards in READY status, ensuring continuous evaluation of event-generating control gaps across the account.`

    impl_KSI_MLA_OSM `Audit record content requirements are satisfied by GuardDuty findings, which include resource identity, threat type, severity, timestamp, and affected asset. Finding publishing frequency is validated at FIFTEEN_MINUTES to ensure near-real-time delivery. Security Hub aggregates findings across all regions (ALL_REGIONS linking mode) into a single pane, satisfying centralized logging requirements.`

    impl_KSI_MLA_RVL `Log review is operationalized by validating that GuardDuty is actively publishing findings (status PUBLISHING) to the security findings S3 bucket, and that Security Hub is enabled with cross-region aggregation configured. This confirms the infrastructure for continuous automated log review is operational and delivering to the designated review destination.`

    impl_KSI_MLA_OSM `Tamper-resistant log storage is validated by confirming the security findings S3 bucket has: KMS encryption with bucket keys enabled, versioning enabled (Enabled status), all four public access block settings set to true, and a bucket policy with a DenyNonSSL statement enforcing HTTPS-only transport (ssl_enforced = true). These controls collectively satisfy AU-9 protection of audit information.`

    impl_KSI_MLA_LET `Continuous audit record generation is validated by confirming GuardDuty detector status is ENABLED and the publishing destination status is PUBLISHING. This confirms the system is actively generating and delivering security findings to the designated S3 destination on a FIFTEEN_MINUTES frequency.`

    impl_KSI_MLA_OSM `System monitoring is validated by confirming GuardDuty is enabled with S3_DATA_EVENTS and EBS_MALWARE_PROTECTION features active, providing continuous monitoring for data exfiltration and malware. Security Hub auto_enable_controls is validated as true, ensuring new controls are automatically evaluated as standards are updated.`

    impl_KSI_MLA_OSM `Transmission confidentiality for audit data is validated by confirming the security findings S3 bucket enforces HTTPS-only access via a bucket policy DenyNonSSL statement (ssl_enforced = true) and uses KMS encryption (sse_algorithm = aws:kms) for data at rest. The publishing destination KMS key ARN is validated to confirm findings are encrypted in transit to and at rest in the bucket.`

META_END

DEF
    # ==========================================================================
    # Variables
    # ==========================================================================
    VAR aws_region string `us-east-1`
    VAR guardduty_detector_id string `00000000000000000000000000000000`
    VAR security_bucket_name string `example-org-security-findings`
    VAR security_bucket_kms_arn string `arn:aws:kms:us-east-1:123456789012:key/example-key-id-0000-0000-000000000000`

    # ==========================================================================
    # Objects
    # ==========================================================================

    OBJECT main_detector
        detector_id VAR guardduty_detector_id
        region VAR aws_region
    OBJECT_END

    OBJECT security_hub
        region VAR aws_region
    OBJECT_END

    OBJECT security_findings_bucket
        bucket_name VAR security_bucket_name
        region VAR aws_region
    OBJECT_END

    # ==========================================================================
    # States
    # ==========================================================================

    # GuardDuty: enabled with required features, publishing to encrypted destination
    STATE guardduty_compliant
        found boolean = true
        status string = `ENABLED`
        finding_publishing_frequency string = `FIFTEEN_MINUTES`
        feature_cloud_trail string = `ENABLED`
        feature_dns_logs string = `ENABLED`
        feature_flow_logs string = `ENABLED`
        feature_s3_data_events string = `ENABLED`
        feature_ebs_malware_protection string = `ENABLED`
        has_publishing_destination boolean = true
        publishing_destination_status string = `PUBLISHING`
        publishing_destination_type string = `S3`
    STATE_END

    # GuardDuty destination: delivering to the correct KMS-encrypted bucket
    STATE guardduty_destination_compliant
        found boolean = true
        publishing_destination_arn string = `arn:aws:s3:::example-org-security-findings`
        publishing_destination_kms_key_arn string starts VAR security_bucket_kms_arn
    STATE_END

    # Security Hub: enabled, required standards active, cross-region aggregation
    STATE securityhub_compliant
        found boolean = true
        auto_enable_controls boolean = true
        standard_fsbp_enabled boolean = true
        standard_nist_800_53_enabled boolean = true
        standards_count int >= 2
        has_finding_aggregator boolean = true
        finding_aggregator_region_linking_mode string = `ALL_REGIONS`
    STATE_END

    # Security findings bucket: tamper-resistant, encrypted, SSL-enforced
    STATE security_bucket_compliant
        found boolean = true
        versioning_status string = `Enabled`
        sse_algorithm string = `aws:kms`
        bucket_key_enabled boolean = true
        block_public_acls boolean = true
        ignore_public_acls boolean = true
        block_public_policy boolean = true
        restrict_public_buckets boolean = true
        lifecycle_enabled boolean = true
        has_bucket_policy boolean = true
        ssl_enforced boolean = true
    STATE_END

    # ==========================================================================
    # Criteria
    # ==========================================================================
    CRI AND
        # GuardDuty detector enabled with required monitoring features
        CTN aws_guardduty_detector
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF guardduty_compliant
            OBJECT_REF main_detector
        CTN_END

        # GuardDuty publishing to correct encrypted destination
        CTN aws_guardduty_detector
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF guardduty_destination_compliant
            OBJECT_REF main_detector
        CTN_END

        # Security Hub enabled with FSBP, NIST 800-53, and cross-region aggregation
        CTN aws_securityhub_account
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF securityhub_compliant
            OBJECT_REF security_hub
        CTN_END

        # Security findings bucket tamper-resistant and encrypted
        CTN aws_s3_bucket
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF security_bucket_compliant
            OBJECT_REF security_findings_bucket
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
